# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# dreamwork target-repo .gitignore — copy these lines into YOUR project's
# .gitignore when running the dreamwork loop on it.
#
# Every entry below is MACHINE-LOCAL runtime state (the C1 trust boundary):
# it describes what THIS machine's loop has seen or done, not project content.
# Committing any of them would export one machine's history into every clone.
#
# Project content that SHOULD be committed (never gitignored):
#   .dreamwork/tasks.md         — the task ledger (or the store migration notice)
#   .dreamwork/questions.md     — open questions for the human
#   .dreamwork/answers.md       — answered questions (archive)
#   .dreamwork/handoffs.md      — work landed outside the ledger, pending fold
#   .dreamwork/lessons.md       — running lessons log
#   .dreamwork/dreams/          — dream entries (memory from earlier sessions)
#   .dreamwork/docs/            — living docs maintained by the dreamers
#   DREAMWORK.md                — project goals, philosophy, preferences
#
# This file is itself committed in the dreamwork SKILL repo so users can
# discover it. See file-formats.md for each file's shape and contract.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# the loop's per-tick status snapshot — describes a running process, stale the
# moment the session ends
.dreamwork/status.json

# lint.py's memo of which status.json keys this target has carried — describes
# a gitignored file and is per-target by construction
.dreamwork/.status-keys

# derived at plugin resolution; which plugins resolve is a property of the
# machine, so a committed copy would be another target's truth
.dreamwork/plugin-commands.json

# dashboard actions (answers, commands, run-mode) as they arrived — a recovery
# record for the human, not project history
.dreamwork/watch-events.log

# every submission as it arrived, raw and unvalidated — ephemeral recovery, and
# it holds whatever the human typed, so it is the last file that should be pushed
.dreamwork/submissions.log

# durable user-event journal — machine-local per target; holds exact payload bytes
# (WAL and SHM sidecars share the prefix)
.dreamwork/user-events.sqlite3
.dreamwork/user-events.sqlite3-wal
.dreamwork/user-events.sqlite3-shm

# the ledger store — machine-local (same trust boundary as the journal);
# cross-clone history is the committed text export, a later deployment choice
.dreamwork/ledger.sqlite3
.dreamwork/ledger.sqlite3-wal
.dreamwork/ledger.sqlite3-shm
.dreamwork/migration-backup/

# main-dreamer pace for this host — operational posture, not a portable default
.dreamwork/run-mode

# the dashboard's per-entry "when did this question last change" store — records
# what THIS dashboard has seen
.dreamwork/question-sigs.json

# the ledger-lint hook's last-seen mtime snapshot — records what THIS machine's
# hook has seen
.dreamwork/.ledger-lint-mtimes.json

# the posture axes — describes THIS host's posture, not the project's
.dreamwork/posture

# the free-text subagent policy override — same argument; the standing
# default is committed in lint.py, so ignoring this loses nothing
.dreamwork/subagent-policy

# the coordinator inbox — every line points at a report under /tmp, worthless
# the moment the session ends
.dreamwork/inbox.md

# the applied-ledger — consume writes one marker per drained receipt (the
# exactly-once proof); the .lock is the mutex held during a drain
.dreamwork/applied.md
.dreamwork/applied.md.lock

# the topic-chat transcript store — append-only turns per chat; machine-local
# conversational truth (a cross-clone export is a later explicit act)
.dreamwork/chats-v1/

# worktrees for isolated dreamer spikes
.worktrees/

# harness-local runtime state — task backends and browser automation are
# session ephemera, not project content
.pi/
.playwright-mcp/
